<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Sforza</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sforza family, Sforza dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sforza were an Italian family of condottieri who ruled the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 1450 to 1535, with interruptions. Founded by Muzio Attendolo, called Sforza, the dynasty rose when his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-sforza">Francesco Sforza</a> married the last Visconti heiress and became duke. Branches also ruled Pesaro and other towns, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludovico-sforza">Ludovico Sforza</a> the Milanese court was among the most brilliant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-sforza.jpg" alt="House of Sforza" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heralder, Eagle by Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_House_of_Sforza.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
